response.output:
# Lending Desk Domain Model

I picked **Patron** and **Loan** because they're the most specific terms and are the words the rest of the model needs. The other words become aliases to avoid in code and conversation.

## Ubiquitous Language

| Term | Definition | Avoid |
|---|---|---|
| **Patron** | A person registered with the library who may borrow items. | borrower, member, user, customer |
| **Item** | A physical copy the library can lend. | copy, book, title |
| **Loan** | The record of one Item lent to one Patron, from lending until return. | checkout, circulation, borrowing |
| **Lend** (verb) | To create a Loan by giving an Item to a Patron. | check out |
| **Return** (verb) | To close a Loan by taking the Item back. | check in |
| **Renewal** | Extending an open Loan's due date. Counted against the policy. | extension |
| **Due Date** | The date by which an open Loan's Item must be returned. | deadline, return date |
| **Overdue** | An open Loan whose Due Date has passed. | late |
| **Patron Status** | Whether a Patron may borrow: `Active`, `Suspended`, or `Expired`. | |
| **Loan Policy** | The rules for lending: loan length, maximum renewals, and maximum open Loans per Patron. | rules, settings |

If the library also tracks membership cards or fees as a separate concept, that belongs in another bounded context. Inside the lending context, "member" means Patron.

## Aggregates

- **Patron** (root). Invariant: may borrow only when `Active`.
- **Item** (root). Invariant: `OnLoan` if and only if it has exactly one open Loan. It owns this rule, so it can't be lent twice.
- **Loan** (root). References Item and Patron by id only. Invariants: renewals never exceed the policy, and a returned Loan can't be returned again.

## Sketch in Scala

```scala
import cats.effect.IO
import java.time.LocalDate
import java.util.UUID

final case class PatronId(value: UUID)
final case class ItemId(value: UUID)
final case class LoanId(value: UUID)

enum PatronStatus { case Active, Suspended, Expired }
enum ItemStatus   { case OnShelf, OnLoan, Lost, Withdrawn }

final case class LoanPolicy(loanDays: Int, maxRenewals: Int, maxOpenLoans: Int)

sealed trait LendingError
final case class PatronCannotBorrow(id: PatronId)  extends LendingError
final case class LoanLimitReached(id: PatronId)    extends LendingError
final case class ItemUnavailable(id: ItemId)       extends LendingError
final case class RenewalLimitReached(id: LoanId)   extends LendingError
final case class LoanAlreadyClosed(id: LoanId)     extends LendingError
final case class CannotRenewOverdue(id: LoanId)    extends LendingError

final case class Patron(id: PatronId, status: PatronStatus) {
  def canBorrow: Boolean = status == PatronStatus.Active
}

// Aggregate root: owns the "one open loan per item" invariant
final case class Item(id: ItemId, status: ItemStatus) {
  def lend: Either[LendingError, Item] = status match {
    case ItemStatus.OnShelf => Right(copy(status = ItemStatus.OnLoan))
    case _                  => Left(ItemUnavailable(id))
  }
  def returned: Item = copy(status = ItemStatus.OnShelf)
}

// Aggregate root: references other aggregates by id only
final case class Loan(
    id: LoanId,
    itemId: ItemId,
    patronId: PatronId,
    lentOn: LocalDate,
    dueOn: LocalDate,
    renewals: Int,
    returnedOn: Option[LocalDate]
) {
  def isOpen: Boolean = returnedOn.isEmpty
  def isOverdue(today: LocalDate): Boolean = isOpen && today.isAfter(dueOn)

  def renew(today: LocalDate, policy: LoanPolicy): Either[LendingError, Loan] =
    if (!isOpen) Left(LoanAlreadyClosed(id))
    else if (isOverdue(today)) Left(CannotRenewOverdue(id))
    else if (renewals >= policy.maxRenewals) Left(RenewalLimitReached(id))
    else Right(copy(dueOn = today.plusDays(policy.loanDays.toLong), renewals = renewals + 1))

  def close(today: LocalDate): Either[LendingError, Loan] =
    if (!isOpen) Left(LoanAlreadyClosed(id))
    else Right(copy(returnedOn = Some(today)))
}

// Domain service: pure, so the rules are testable without infrastructure
object LendingDesk {
  def lend(
      patron: Patron,
      item: Item,
      openLoansForPatron: Int,
      today: LocalDate,
      policy: LoanPolicy,
      newLoanId: LoanId
  ): Either[LendingError, (Item, Loan)] =
    for {
      _    <- Either.cond(patron.canBorrow, (), PatronCannotBorrow(patron.id))
      _    <- Either.cond(openLoansForPatron < policy.maxOpenLoans, (), LoanLimitReached(patron.id))
